  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw400.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 406.29 Modifications and Expansions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 406.29 Modifications and Expansions.\n\n(a) Any person seeking to expand a non-community PWS shall submit the following to the department:\n\n(1) Historical water use data for at least the past 2 years;\n\n(2) The proposed design flow calculated in accordance with Env-Dw 406.11; and\n\n(3) Documentation demonstrating the existing source(s) have the required supply capacity as required by Env-Dw 406.12.\n\n(b) Any person seeking to modify or expand a PWS in accordance with Env-Dw 406.05 shall submit the following to the department:\n\n(1) A written request to amend the design approval;\n\n(2) A description of the necessary changes;\n\n(3) An explanation of why the changes are needed;\n\n(4) Plan sheets, including revisions to previously approved plans, and the following, if applicable:\n\na. For new well(s), the information in Env-Dw 406.13 through 406.16;\n\nb. For storage tank(s), the information in Env-Dw 406.20;\n\nc. For pump controls and auxiliary equipment, the information in Env-Dw 406.18;\n\nd. For a pumphouse or pump room, the information in Env-Dw 406.17;\n\ne. For well appurtenances and pumps, the information in Env-Dw 406.19;\n\nf. For wiring and control devices, the information in Env-Dw 406.21;\n\ng. For water treatment facilities, the information in Env-Dw 406.22, 406.23, and 406.25; and\n\nh. For water distribution systems, the information in Env-Dw 406.26;\n\n(5) Revised calculations, as applicable;\n\n(6) If infrastructure is decommissioned, photo documentation showing a minimum 12-inch gap in the piping from the original well(s), storage tank(s), and any other decommissioned infrastructure;\n\n(7) If connection to another PWS is proposed, documentation from the supplying owner certifying that:\n\na. Adequate quantities of water are available to serve the proposed PWS; and\n\nb. With the proposed PWS online, adequate system pressures and source capacity will be maintained; and\n\n(8) The design fee as required by Env Dw-402.03.\n\n(c) For deepening or hydrofracturing of wells, the applicant shall submit:\n\n(1) The well capacity after hydrofracturing or deepening determined pursuant to Env-Dw 406.15; and\n\n(2) The water quality analysis results of the water from each well as specified in Env-Dw 406.16.\n\n(d) Replacement in-kind does not require department approval, except that replacement of a well shall comply with the requirements of Env-Dw 406.13 through Env-Dw 406.16.\n\n(e) The plans and specifications for modifications to PWSs having a design flow greater than 20,000 gpd shall be sealed by a professional civil or sanitary engineer licensed in the state of New Hampshire.\n\n(f) The department shall approve the application to modify the non-community PWS if the design meets the criteria in this part.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at part heading for Env-Dw 405) #10612, eff 6-1-14\n\nNew. #14158, eff 12-25-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw400.html"
